    {
      "id": "52d4cf8e52a28c5e410122ddccecf6727e533c4a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2001219589,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I attempted to install npcap 1.79 to my Win 10 22H2 system that had Wireshark 4.2.6 with npcap 1.78 and the system froze solid with the npcap installer displaying the \"Installing NDIS filter ...\" message.\n\nEventually the system bluescreened (first in a very long time) and the bugcheck was DPC_WATCHDOG_VIOLATION (0x133).\n\nAfter the bluescreen restart, npcap didn't appear to be installed, installed 1.79 again, all went OK, and Wireshark was able to capture traffic.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
